# See https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file for more about ignoring files.

# Ignore git directory.
/.git/
/.gitignore

# Ignore bundler config.
/.bundle

# Ignore all environment files.
/.env*

# Ignore all default key files.
/config/master.key
/config/credentials/*.key

# Ignore all logfiles and tempfiles.
/log/*
/tmp/*
!/log/.keep
!/tmp/.keep

# Ignore pidfiles, but keep the directory.
/tmp/pids/*
!/tmp/pids/.keep

# Ignore storage (uploaded files in development and any SQLite databases).
/storage/*
!/storage/.keep
/tmp/storage/*
!/tmp/storage/.keep

# Ignore assets.
/node_modules/
/app/assets/builds/*
!/app/assets/builds/.keep
/public/assets

# Ignore CI service files.
/.github

# Ignore Kamal files.
/config/deploy*.yml
/.kamal

# Ignore development files
/.devcontainer

# Ignore Docker-related files
/.dockerignore
/Dockerfile*

# ── Developer-machine artefacts that must never reach the image (#862) ────────
# CI builds from a clean checkout, so these are invisible there — but a local
# `docker build` copies whatever is in the working tree. A developer who has run
# the ui-smoke suite ships Playwright's bundled `node` binary (3 CVEs, and it is
# not a SPARC dependency at all), and an agent worktree under .claude/ bakes an
# entire second copy of the repository into the production image. Both were
# observed in a local build of v1.15.3 and neither is present in the published
# image, which is exactly the local-vs-CI drift that hides prod-only bugs.
/.claude/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

/coverage/

# NOTE: /spec/ is deliberately NOT excluded. lib/tasks/catalog_oscal_id_migration.rake
# and lib/tasks/profile_backfill.rake load catalog fixtures from
# spec/fixtures/files/catalogs/ at runtime, so dropping spec/ would break those
# data-migration tasks inside the container. Slimming the image further means
# relocating those fixtures out of spec/ first — worth doing, but it is a
# behaviour change and does not belong in this commit.

# ── Non-runtime content must not ship (#1080) ────────────────────────────────
#
# `docs/hdf/` is GITIGNORED — its files are local-only scan output. But
# `.dockerignore` did not exclude it, so `COPY . .` baked a developer's own
# 556 KB CycloneDX SBOM into their locally-built image, and **Trivy's image scan
# parses SBOM files it
# finds on the filesystem and merges their components as installed packages** —
# so the scanner reported that SBOM's 381 stale components as if they were
# installed. Measured on the shipping image: 471 packages reported against 303
# real gemspecs. 105 phantoms, 100 of them the same gem at an older version
# (actioncable 8.1.2 beside the real 8.1.3.1), plus 35 "Go CVEs" attributed to
# `thruster` — a gem REMOVED in #639 that the March SBOM still lists.
#
# That is the whole of #1080, and it is a LOCAL-BUILD defect: CI never had these
# files (they are gitignored), which is why CI correctly reported 0 while local
# reported 68. Proven by control: scanning the same image with
# `--skip-files rails/docs/hdf/trivy-container-local.cdx.json` drops 471 gems to
# 237, and every phantom — both erb versions, rack 3.2.5, actioncable 8.1.2, the
# thruster gobinary target — disappears.
#
# It survived every cache clear, an explicit --platform, a --no-cache rebuild and
# even flattening the image to one layer, because the file is genuinely in the
# artifact. An empty directory scanned clean because it had no SBOM in it.
#
# THE GENERAL RULE: .dockerignore must exclude what .gitignore excludes, or a
# local-only artifact silently changes what a locally-built image contains — and
# local scans stop matching CI.
#
# Neither directory is read at runtime (verified: the `docs/` mentions in app/
# are comments). Excluding them removes ~35 MB and stops the scanner ingesting
# our own stale evidence as fact.
#
# NOT excluding /spec/ here despite its 64 MB: lib/tasks/profile_backfill.rake
# and lib/tasks/catalog_oscal_id_migration.rake read
# spec/fixtures/files/catalogs/NIST_SP-800-53_rev4_catalog.json, so a blanket
# exclusion would break those data migrations. Tracked separately.
/docs/
/tests/
